  "title": "9's Complement Generator of a BCD Digit (No Inverter)",
  "description": "Design a circuit that outputs the 9's complement (9 - N) of a BCD digit N (N3 N2 N1 N0, range 0-9) using one 7483 IC and XOR gates. You are NOT allowed to use a 7404 inverter. Hint: 9 - N = 1001 + N' + 1. Obtain N' by XOR-ing each bit with logic 1 (Vcc), put 1001 on the A inputs and tie the Carry-In to logic 1. This block is the first step of building a BCD subtractor.",
